  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is Arduino Uno. Provided pin wiring roles used exactly: A0 soil moisture ADC, A1 rain ADC, A2 water level ADC, D10 pump relay, D13 status LED, D6 buzzer, D2 button, TM1637 CLK=D4 DIO=D5.",
    "No explicit electrical polarity (e.g., pullup/button active-low, pump relay active-high) was specified. Digital input/output initial/model polarity must be handled by SysML (these requests use default catalog behavior; the application must interpret the meaning/model values consistently).",
    "Soil moisture / rain / water level thresholds and mapping from ADC to 'dry'/'not raining'/'water sufficient' are business/model parameters not specified; must be implemented in SysML.",
    "TM1637 number displays a single integer that the model updates while cycling between soil moisture, water level, and current mode. Exact formatting, scaling/rounding to fit TM1637 range, and cycling order are business/model logic.",
    "Serial reporting protocol (baud and framing) was not specified; a single reporting baud of 9600 with line framing default is assumed via catalog defaults. Report cadence and which specific report condition gates the trigger are decided in SysML."
